{
  // Terrain rules (docs/design.md, "Terrain"): movement classes, matched in order; a unit takes
  // the last class whose locomotor matches and whose minRadius (tenths of a cell) it reaches.
  // Slopes are percent grade where Gentle, Steep and Cliff begin; speeds and forest values are
  // percents per slope class [flat, gentle, steep, cliff] or forest density [none, scrub, grove,
  // dense]; maxRadius (optional) the largest radius a class applies to; path cost per cell with open flat ground at 10, 0 = impassable; uphillCost is the
  // extra percent for a climbing step (centre to centre) from uphillFull percent grade of the step's length on, nothing under
  // uphillFrom (the dead zone: the ground's small bumps, 10 cm a cell, cost nothing), a share in between (the engine's
  // docs/design.md, "Straight routes"); roadSpeed and roadCost the percent of a road cell's speed
  // and cost (of the same cell off-road; slope and forest still apply) per road kind [highway,
  // paved, gravel, dirt] (a single roadCost number means every kind). The two foot kinds, alley
  // (foot class only: a wall to the rest) and footpath, have no values of their own: the foot
  // class pays its paved road cost on them and gets no speed change, every other class pays and
  // gets nothing (docs/design.md, "Alleys and footpaths"). A vehicle's road costs are the time a road really saves (100 over
  // its roadSpeed), so a road is taken only when the detour to it pays (docs/design.md, "Straight routes").
  // shortTrip (optional; cells): a trip no longer than this ignores roads (they cost as the ground beside them), except where one
  // lies within shortTripRoad cells of the straight line and the way along it costs at least shortTripSaving percent less;
  // deployMaxGrade (optional, default the steep threshold) the grade from which launchers of
  // the class can't set up (wheels: 15, so a 15-25% slope they drive on is still too steep). Not part of
  // content/mvp: these only take part in (and are hashed with) games on a map with terrain, so
  // flat maps are unchanged. Starting values for the owner to tune.
  // Tree trunks (docs/design.md, "Trees as obstacles"; decisions 439 to 450): trunks says what a standing tree trunk is to
  // the class: "ignore" (infantry walk between them and over fallen ones), "avoid" (a wall: jeeps and light trucks steer
  // between trees, if the gaps fit them) or "push" (tanks and heavy trucks push it over: pushCost is the path cost of a
  // trunk's cell in percent of the same cell without one, pushSpeedPercent their top speed while pushing, pushTicks the
  // contact it takes; the tree falls the way they face). crossFallen: a pusher rolls over a fallen trunk at its push speed
  // and cost (otherwise it is a wall to it; to the other vehicles it always is). forestCost and forestSpeed are the
  // undergrowth between the trunks, so the pushers have no forestBlockedFrom any more; dense forest is shut to the cars
  // (forestBlockedFrom 3): its trunks leave them no way across, only pockets a crowd of them wedges in.
  // Forest fire (docs/design.md, "Forest fire"; content/mvp/fire.json): fireCost is the path cost of a burning cell in percent
  // of the same cell not burning, 0 (the default) a wall while it burns: vehicles never drive into fire (one standing in a cell
  // that catches drives out); infantry (100: their routes ignore fire) walk out of it on their own when it burns them.
  // thinnedForestAsBefore: a cell whose forest fire burnt or a blast thinned a level down keeps its old forest's cost and speed
  // for the class: infantry pick their way through snags and stumps as through the wood, so neither changes their routing
  // (rebuilding infantry routing round a moving fire front cost about 15 ms a batch on the fire bench); vehicles get the lighter
  // forest (a burnt dense wood is a grove to them: the cars may enter it).
  // lips (docs/design.md, "Straight routes"): for movement a cell's grade is the rise over a window of that many cells round it
  // (the steepest way across, per cell), or over a window two cells narrower less slack percent if that is more: a sustained
  // slope keeps its class, a short bank (2 m in 3 or 4 cells) stays steep, and a short step reads as what it is in the ground
  // around it. A cell that itself rises more than rise percent (a step of 80 cm over its 2 m) keeps its own grade: a wall stays
  // a wall. Building, deploying and sight read the cell's own grade.
  "lips": { "window": 5, "rise": 40, "slack": 4 },
  "classes": [
    { "id": "foot", "locomotor": "foot", "slopes": { "gentle": 10, "steep": 25, "cliff": 45 },
      "speedUp": [100, 85, 60, 0], "speedDown": [100, 105, 90, 0], "cost": [10, 12, 18, 0], "uphillCost": 30, "uphillFrom": 5, "uphillFull": 10,
      "roadCost": [90, 90, 90, 90], "roadSpeed": [100, 100, 100, 100], "forestCost": [100, 100, 110, 120], "forestSpeed": [100, 100, 95, 90], "forestBlockedFrom": 4,
      "trunks": "ignore", "fireCost": 100, "thinnedForestAsBefore": true },
    { "id": "wheeled", "locomotor": "wheeled", "slopes": { "gentle": 10, "steep": 25, "cliff": 45 },
      "speedUp": [100, 75, 0, 0], "speedDown": [100, 100, 0, 0], "cost": [10, 14, 0, 0], "uphillCost": 50, "uphillFrom": 5, "uphillFull": 10,
      "roadCost": [71, 80, 91, 100], "roadSpeed": [140, 125, 110, 100], "shortTrip": 180, "shortTripRoad": 5, "shortTripSaving": 10, "forestCost": [100, 130, 170, 250], "forestSpeed": [100, 85, 60, 40], "forestBlockedFrom": 3,
      "deployMaxGrade": 15, "trunks": "avoid", "fireCost": 0 },
    // Light 4x4s (the technical, the rocket jeep, the dirt bike: radius 0.8 cell and down) climb
    // what infantry can up to 40% grade, at half speed on Steep ground.
    { "id": "light_wheeled", "locomotor": "wheeled", "maxRadius": 8, "slopes": { "gentle": 10, "steep": 25, "cliff": 41 },
      "speedUp": [100, 80, 50, 0], "speedDown": [100, 100, 70, 0], "cost": [10, 13, 25, 0], "uphillCost": 50, "uphillFrom": 5, "uphillFull": 10,
      "roadCost": [71, 80, 91, 100], "roadSpeed": [140, 125, 110, 100], "shortTrip": 180, "shortTripRoad": 5, "shortTripSaving": 10, "forestCost": [100, 130, 170, 250], "forestSpeed": [100, 85, 60, 40], "forestBlockedFrom": 3,
      "deployMaxGrade": 15, "trunks": "avoid", "fireCost": 0 },
    // Heavy wheeled vehicles (the trucks: radius 1 cell and up) push trees over, slowly; dense undergrowth slows them most.
    { "id": "heavy_wheeled", "locomotor": "wheeled", "minRadius": 10, "slopes": { "gentle": 10, "steep": 25, "cliff": 45 },
      "speedUp": [100, 70, 0, 0], "speedDown": [100, 100, 0, 0], "cost": [10, 15, 0, 0], "uphillCost": 60, "uphillFrom": 5, "uphillFull": 10,
      "roadCost": [71, 80, 91, 100], "roadSpeed": [140, 125, 110, 100], "shortTrip": 180, "shortTripRoad": 5, "shortTripSaving": 10, "forestCost": [100, 140, 200, 280], "forestSpeed": [100, 80, 50, 35],
      "deployMaxGrade": 15, "trunks": "push", "pushCost": 300, "pushSpeedPercent": 30, "pushTicks": 30, "crossFallen": true, "fireCost": 0 },
    // The bulldozer alone ("only"): the tracked class's ground, but built for trees (the owner, 2026-11-07: "much faster than a
    // regular truck or vehicle ... they fall as it walks, not too fast but fast enough"). A trunk falls after 0.5 s of contact
    // (tanks 1.5 s), it holds 60% of its top speed while it pushes (tanks 30%) and its routes hardly pay for woods or trunks, so it
    // goes straight through. Decisions 960 to 962.
    { "id": "dozer", "locomotor": "tracked", "only": ["bulldozer"], "slopes": { "gentle": 10, "steep": 25, "cliff": 45 },
      "speedUp": [100, 85, 60, 0], "speedDown": [100, 100, 90, 0], "cost": [10, 12, 20, 0], "uphillCost": 40, "uphillFrom": 5, "uphillFull": 10,
      "roadCost": [91, 91, 95, 100], "roadSpeed": [110, 110, 105, 100], "shortTrip": 180, "shortTripRoad": 5, "shortTripSaving": 10, "forestCost": [100, 100, 105, 110], "forestSpeed": [100, 100, 90, 80],
      "trunks": "push", "pushCost": 100, "pushSpeedPercent": 60, "pushTicks": 10, "crossFallen": true, "fireCost": 0 },
    { "id": "tracked", "locomotor": "tracked", "slopes": { "gentle": 10, "steep": 25, "cliff": 45 },
      "speedUp": [100, 85, 60, 0], "speedDown": [100, 100, 90, 0], "cost": [10, 12, 20, 0], "uphillCost": 40, "uphillFrom": 5, "uphillFull": 10,
      "roadCost": [91, 91, 95, 100], "roadSpeed": [110, 110, 105, 100], "shortTrip": 180, "shortTripRoad": 5, "shortTripSaving": 10, "forestCost": [100, 110, 140, 180], "forestSpeed": [100, 95, 75, 60],
      "trunks": "push", "pushCost": 300, "pushSpeedPercent": 30, "pushTicks": 30, "crossFallen": true, "fireCost": 0 }
  ],
  // The trunks: trunkChance is the chance in percent that a 2 x 2 block of forest cells holds one standing trunk, per
  // density [none, scrub, grove, dense] (scrub is bushes only); a fallen trunk covers fallenLengthCells cells from its stump
  // along its fall and lies fallenTicks (600: 30 s) before it is gone. The trunks are worked out from the forest
  // (TreeTrunks in Sim/Trees.cs), the same on every machine. Starting values for the owner to tune.
  // Strikes blow trees down (decisions 451 to 457): a blast whose warhead is in fell blows down every standing trunk within
  // that percent of its weapon's splash radius (never under fellMinRadius, tenths of a cell: an anti-tank missile has no
  // splash), each falling away from the impact and lying as a pushed one does. Small warheads (rockets, anti-tank and helicopter
  // missiles, a drone's grenade) fell 1 or 2 trees in dense forest, shells a small clearing, bombs (half their splash: 2.5 to
  // 6.5 cells) a ring each and a carpet a lane. Bullets, cannon, darts, air-to-air missiles and the anti-personnel mine fell
  // nothing. A trunk falling across a cell takes fallDamage percent of max HP from the units with fallDamageTags standing
  // there (infantry), once; vehicles nothing yet. blastThins: a cell whose tree a blast blew down loses one forest level, so
  // a bombed wood opens sight lines there (forest fire drops a burnt cell's level too; docs/design.md, "Forest fire").
  "trees": { "trunkChance": [0, 0, 50, 85], "fallenLengthCells": 4, "fallenTicks": 600,
    "fell": { "rocket": 100, "atgm": 100, "heli_missile": 100, "explosive": 100, "at_blast": 100, "mortar_bomb": 100,
      "he_mpat": 100, "heavy_cannon": 100, "air_strike": 100, "mrl_rocket": 100, "heavy_rocket": 100, "bunker_buster": 100,
      "crash": 100, "drone_charge": 60, "kaman_charge": 60, "heavy_missile": 50, "ballistic": 50, "bomb": 50 },
    "fellMinRadius": 15, "fallDamage": 10, "fallDamageTags": ["infantry"], "blastThins": true },
  // Fog of war (setups with "fog": true): line of sight for ground units. Heights in tenths of a
  // metre: eyes (soldiers 1.7 m, vehicles 2.5 m; structures and garrisons see from their roof),
  // the height a target must show above its cell's ground, and the canopy per forest density
  // [none, scrub, grove, dense] that raises what blocks sight. forestSight is what each forest
  // cell a sight line crosses costs; a cell is hidden once the sum reaches forestBudget: you see
  // about 8 cells (16 m) into scrub, 4 into a grove and 2 into dense forest. Air units see over
  // ridges and woods, but under the trees only as their sensors allow (content/mvp/concealment.json:
  // concealment from the air). Starting values for the owner to tune.
  "vision": { "eyeFoot": 17, "eyeVehicle": 25, "target": 15, "canopy": [0, 20, 60, 100],
    "forestSight": [0, 1, 2, 4], "forestBudget": 8 },
  // Spotting (fog phase F4e; the engine's docs/design.md, "Spotting"; decisions 859 to 875): seeing a cell is not spotting the
  // unit in it. With fog of war on a terrain map, a ground observer spots an enemy soldier or vehicle out on the map only when
  // its cell is in the observer's own sight (the rays above) and the level distance is within
  //   sight x optics x concealment x cover[state] / 100^3,
  // a percent of 100 or more: wherever it sees the cell. concealment per kind of unit (a decoy is its disguise's kind); optics per
  // observer archetype (any other: 100); cover per kind [still, moving, fired]: open, scrub, grove, dense, and town (open ground
  // or scrub beside a standing building); fired: a unit that fired within that many ticks (5 s). Infantry (40): in the open
  // spotted wherever seen; still in a grove within 30% of the sight (a rifleman's 10.5 cells: 3.15), moving 60%, firing 100%; dense
  // 20 / 40 / 100%; beside a building 50 / 80 / 100%. A tank (100) still in a grove within 75%. Air units keep concealment.json
  // (canopy) and see the open and scrub as before; the town row and their optics apply to them.
  // The woods (the owner, 2026-11-02): an observer standing in the woods (grove or dense) sees woodsSight percent as far over
  // woods cells (open cells at its sight), and the forest budget does not hold along a line that has not left the woods.
  "spotting": {
    "concealment": { "foot": 40, "wheeled": 70, "tracked": 100 },
    "optics": { "sniper": 150, "observation_post": 150, "overseer_drone": 150 },
    "cover": { "open": [250, 250, 250], "scrub": [150, 200, 250], "grove": [75, 150, 250], "dense": [50, 100, 250],
      "town": [125, 200, 250] },
    "fired": 100,
    "woods": [false, false, true, true], "woodsSight": 150 }
}
